      "data": {
        "id": "chatPromptTemplate_0",
        "label": "Chat Prompt Template",
        "version": 2,
        "name": "chatPromptTemplate",
        "type": "ChatPromptTemplate",
        "baseClasses": [
          "ChatPromptTemplate",
          "BaseChatPromptTemplate",
          "BasePromptTemplate",
          "Runnable"
        ],
        "category": "Prompts",
        "description": "Schema to represent a chat prompt",
        "inputParams": [
          {
            "label": "System Message",
            "name": "systemMessagePrompt",
            "type": "string",
            "rows": 4,
            "placeholder": "You are a helpful assistant that translates {input_language} to {output_language}.",
            "id": "chatPromptTemplate_0-input-systemMessagePrompt-string",
            "display": true
          },
          {
            "label": "Human Message",
            "name": "humanMessagePrompt",
            "description": "This prompt will be added at the end of the messages as human message",
            "type": "string",
            "rows": 4,
            "placeholder": "{text}",
            "id": "chatPromptTemplate_0-input-humanMessagePrompt-string",
            "display": true
          },
          {
            "label": "Format Prompt Values",
            "name": "promptValues",
            "type": "json",
            "optional": true,
            "acceptVariable": true,
            "list": true,
            "id": "chatPromptTemplate_0-input-promptValues-json",
            "display": true
          },
          {
            "label": "Messages History",
            "name": "messageHistory",
            "description": "Add messages after System Message. This is useful when you want to provide few shot examples",
            "type": "tabs",
            "tabIdentifier": "selectedMessagesTab",
            "additionalParams": true,
            "default": "messageHistoryCode",
            "tabs": [
              {
                "label": "Add Messages (Code)",
                "name": "messageHistoryCode",
                "type": "code",
                "hideCodeExecute": true,
                "codeExample": "const { AIMessage, HumanMessage, ToolMessage } = require('@langchain/core/messages');\n\nreturn [\n    new HumanMessage(\"What is 333382 🦜 1932?\"),\n    new AIMessage({\n        content: \"\",\n        tool_calls: [\n        {\n            id: \"12345\",\n            name: \"calculator\",\n            args: {\n                number1: 333382,\n                number2: 1932,\n                operation: \"divide\",\n            },\n        },\n        ],\n    }),\n    new ToolMessage({\n        tool_call_id: \"12345\",\n        content: \"The answer is 172.558.\",\n    }),\n    new AIMessage(\"The answer is 172.558.\"),\n]",
                "optional": true,
                "additionalParams": true
              }
            ],
            "id": "chatPromptTemplate_0-input-messageHistory-tabs",
            "display": true
          }
        ],
        "inputAnchors": [],
        "inputs": {
          "systemMessagePrompt": "You are a supply chain analytics assistant for BQBYTE Technologies.\nYou have access to two tools:\n\n1. Policy_Retriever\n   - Contains the Supplier Governance Policy.\n   - Use this tool whenever business rules, compliance requirements,\n     rebate eligibility criteria, risk definitions, SLA thresholds,\n     SWL restrictions, disruption response procedures, or escalation\n     policies are required.\n\n2. supplier_sql_query\n   - Contains live supplier performance data in PostgreSQL.\n   - Use this tool whenever supplier records, metrics, counts,\n     aggregations, filtering, averages, rankings, or PO values are required.\n   - Input must be a valid PostgreSQL SELECT query.\n\nSQL table name: supplier_performance\nColumn names (all lowercase):\npo_id, supplier_id, supplier_name, region, country, product_category,\nproduct_sku, unit_cost_usd, lead_time_days, otd_rate_pct, defect_rate_pct,\ncompliance_score, contract_tier, payment_terms_days, moq_units,\nannual_volume_units, risk_level, certifications, last_audit_date,\nsustainability_score, active_disruptions, alt_supplier_id, po_quarter,\nunits_ordered, units_delivered_on_time, units_rejected, po_value_usd.\n\nKey data notes:\n- active_disruptions = 'None' means no disruption; any other value is an active flag\n- contract_tier values: Tier-1, Tier-2, Tier-3\n- risk_level values: Low, Medium, High\n- Always GROUP BY supplier_name when the question asks about suppliers not individual POs\n\nDATA MODEL IMPORTANT:\nThe supplier_performance table contains individual Purchase Order (PO) rows.\nEach supplier has MULTIPLE rows — one per PO transaction.\nColumns like compliance_score, otd_rate_pct, defect_rate_pct, \nsustainability_score are PO-level metrics, not supplier-level.\n\nTherefore:\n- To evaluate a supplier's performance, always AGGREGATE using AVG() \n  and GROUP BY supplier_name\n- Never filter on metric columns directly with WHERE — always aggregate \n  first using HAVING\n- When counting suppliers, count DISTINCT supplier_name values after \n  aggregation, not raw rows\n\nWhen a question depends on policy-defined criteria:\n1. Use Policy Retriever to get the exact rule and thresholds.\n2. Convert the policy rules into explicit SQL filter conditions.\n3. Use supplier_sql_query with a correct PostgreSQL SELECT query.\n4. Combine both results into a final answer citing the policy section.\n\nAlways state which policy section was applied (e.g. \"per Policy §4.2\").\nNever answer numerical questions from memory — always query the database.",
          "humanMessagePrompt": "{input}",
          "promptValues": "",
          "messageHistory": "messageHistoryCode"
        },
        "outputAnchors": [
          {
            "id": "chatPromptTemplate_0-output-chatPromptTemplate-ChatPromptTemplate|BaseChatPromptTemplate|BasePromptTemplate|Runnable",
            "name": "chatPromptTemplate",
            "label": "ChatPromptTemplate",
            "description": "Schema to represent a chat prompt",
            "type": "ChatPromptTemplate | BaseChatPromptTemplate | BasePromptTemplate | Runnable"
          }
        ],
        "outputs": {},
